summary:
  A device that plays alone is reached by the output menu's volume row only
  when a local output is pinned.

history:
  Up to 2026.43 the "Play on" menu's Volume slider and its Mute asked how
  the local sound is routed and nothing else. With the system default
  selected and a television carrying the stream, this computer silent, both
  turned this computer's master and the television heard nothing. Measured
  2026-11-11 on the row's own lines around counting roads: local=1 cast=0,
  and with an output pinned local=0 cast=1. 2026.44 makes the row the
  widget's own volume whenever a device plays alone.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TransportLogic.js

find:
      if (casting === true && localAlong !== true) return "player";

replace:
      if (casting === true && localAlong !== true && followsDefault !== true) return "player";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_a_device_playing_alone_is_what_the_row_turns
  and tests/qml/tst_volumeroad.qml::test_a_television_playing_alone_is_what_the_row_turns.
  Line-neutral.
